WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.210
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.480 --> 01:34.900
The Great Long March

3
01:35.340 --> 01:37.770
[Episode 3]

4
01:38.759 --> 01:39.690
Comrade Zedong,

5
01:40.300 --> 01:41.420
I'd like to explain.

6
01:41.420 --> 01:44.560
[Mao Zedong, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

7
01:42.120 --> 01:45.039
The Red 7th Corps' northward march is to divert the enemy.

8
01:45.039 --> 01:47.970
The Red 6th Corps' westward march is to scout the way.

9
01:48.680 --> 01:50.920
We have to see how the situation develops.

10
01:50.920 --> 01:52.380
It will become clear soon.

11
01:52.590 --> 01:54.050
Please tell Comrade Bo Gu:

12
01:54.110 --> 01:57.240
once a plan is made, a decision must follow immediately.

13
01:57.320 --> 02:01.070
Indecision will lead to a complete loss.

14
02:01.840 --> 02:02.770
Comrade Zedong,

15
02:04.150 --> 02:06.430
the situation is quite complicated now.

16
02:04.970 --> 02:08.759
[Zhou Enlai, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Central Political Bureau Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission General Political Commissar of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

17
02:06.920 --> 02:09.150
I think it's better for you to stay in Ruijin.

18
02:09.150 --> 02:11.410
There's no point in me staying in Ruijin.

19
02:11.840 --> 02:13.570
I'd better go back to Huichang.

20
02:13.750 --> 02:15.430
There's still work to be done there.

21
02:15.430 --> 02:16.800
At the meeting just now,

22
02:16.870 --> 02:18.470
people spoke rather sharply.

23
02:18.470 --> 02:19.960
I hope you won't take it to heart.

24
02:19.960 --> 02:22.190
Enlai, don't make excuses for them.

25
02:22.680 --> 02:24.360
They simply won't let anyone speak up.

26
02:24.360 --> 02:26.640
When Bocheng

27
02:26.829 --> 02:27.950
challenged Li De in Guangchang,

28
02:27.950 --> 02:28.810
Li De stripped him

29
02:28.810 --> 02:31.070
of his post as Chief of the General Staff.

30
02:31.300 --> 02:33.300
Who would dare speak out after that?

31
02:38.320 --> 02:40.130
Mao, here's the umbrella.

32
02:42.650 --> 02:44.850
I have a bamboo hat. I don't need it.

33
02:48.960 --> 02:50.420
Our Red Army's bamboo hats

34
02:50.600 --> 02:52.060
used to have pointed tops.

35
02:52.150 --> 02:53.550
During night marches,

36
02:54.079 --> 02:56.360
anyone at the front who nodded off

37
02:57.120 --> 02:58.560
would bump their head against the point.

38
02:58.470 --> 03:02.060
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission Commander-in-Chief of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

39
02:58.600 --> 03:01.240
I was the one who suggested making the top flat and rounded.

40
03:01.240 --> 03:02.240
It would be safer,

41
03:02.370 --> 03:05.310
and the hats could double as pillows when we slept at night.

42
03:05.310 --> 03:07.370
But not a single experienced craftsman

43
03:07.370 --> 03:08.900
at the hat workshop agreed.

44
03:08.920 --> 03:10.080
Do you know why?

45
03:11.600 --> 03:15.480
They said bamboo hats have always had pointed tops since ancient times.

46
03:15.480 --> 03:17.880
How could they possibly have rounded tops?

47
03:46.000 --> 03:47.110
Comrade Xun Huaizhou.

48
03:47.110 --> 03:47.870
Here!

49
03:48.850 --> 03:50.190
This is the operational directive

50
03:50.190 --> 03:52.800
issued by the Central Revolutionary Military Commission

51
03:52.800 --> 03:55.860
to the Northward Anti-Japanese Expeditionary Force.

52
03:56.800 --> 03:57.680
We hope you will

53
03:57.829 --> 04:00.160
strictly follow the Commission's orders

54
04:00.260 --> 04:02.490
and fulfill the great mission entrusted to you

55
04:02.490 --> 04:04.120
by the Central Committee and the Military Commission.

56
04:04.120 --> 04:05.030
Yes, sir!

57
04:05.120 --> 04:06.770
We will resolutely carry out the Central Committee's decision

58
04:06.670 --> 04:09.520
[Xun Huaizhou, Commander of the Red 7th Army Corps]

59
04:06.930 --> 04:08.760
and complete the task entrusted to us

60
04:08.760 --> 04:13.490
by the Party Central Committee and the Central Revolutionary Military Commission.

61
04:15.340 --> 04:16.850
[Le Shaohua, Political Commissar of the Red 7th Army Corps]

62
04:19.920 --> 04:20.680
Comrades,

63
04:21.600 --> 04:23.330
the evil Japanese imperialism

64
04:23.520 --> 04:26.480
has annexed the Northeast and occupied Rehe.

65
04:27.550 --> 04:30.790
Now they intend to occupy the entire North China.

66
04:31.130 --> 04:32.500
Chiang Kai-shek is not fighting the Japanese.

67
04:32.500 --> 04:34.310
Instead, he mobilized a million-strong army

68
04:34.310 --> 04:36.340
to fight the Communist Party and the Red Army.

69
04:36.340 --> 04:37.890
The Kuomintang wants to betray the country,

70
04:37.890 --> 04:39.610
but we must save it.

71
04:39.960 --> 04:41.460
Chiang Kai-shek is not fighting the Japanese,

72
04:41.460 --> 04:42.900
but our Red Army will.

73
04:43.390 --> 04:44.390
We must drive

74
04:44.740 --> 04:47.540
Japanese imperialism out of China!

75
04:47.630 --> 04:49.780
I will wait for the news of your victory.

76
04:49.780 --> 04:52.470
Drive the Japanese invaders out of China!

77
04:52.680 --> 04:55.920
Drive the Japanese invaders out of China!

78
04:56.700 --> 04:58.970
To draw away and tie down enemy forces,

79
04:59.480 --> 05:01.650
on July 7, 1934,

80
05:02.040 --> 05:03.900
more than 6,000 soldiers of the Red 7th Army Corps

81
05:03.900 --> 05:06.310
set out from Ruijin

82
05:06.330 --> 05:08.160
as the Northward Anti-Japanese Expeditionary Force.

83
05:08.160 --> 05:11.360
They went on to fight across central and northern Fujian,

84
05:11.390 --> 05:13.480
western Zhejiang, and southern Anhui,

85
05:13.480 --> 05:15.610
engaging in frequent fierce battles.

86
05:16.800 --> 05:17.870
Years later,

87
05:18.040 --> 05:19.480
Su Yu recalled,

88
05:20.190 --> 05:22.720
"Under the leadership of Comrades Mao Zedong and Zhu De,

89
05:22.720 --> 05:24.980
I learned how to lead troops and wage war.

90
05:25.190 --> 05:26.640
With unwavering faith

91
05:26.660 --> 05:28.680
in the ultimate victory of the revolution

92
05:28.680 --> 05:31.240
and the determination to overcome every obstacle,

93
05:31.240 --> 05:33.800
I once again embarked on the long road ahead."

94
05:35.500 --> 05:37.750
At a critical moment, when the Chinese Soviet government

95
05:37.750 --> 05:40.360
and the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army

96
05:40.360 --> 05:42.600
were fighting back against the Kuomintang's

97
05:42.230 --> 05:45.560
[Chiang Kai-shek, Generalissimo of the Military Affairs of the Commission of Kuomintang]

98
05:42.620 --> 05:43.650
military encirclement campaigns, they dispatched an advance force

99
05:43.650 --> 05:45.159
northward to fight Japanese imperialism directly,

100
05:45.159 --> 05:47.360
overcoming tremendous difficulties.

101
05:47.480 --> 05:49.600
They also put forward 5 proposals.

102
05:49.630 --> 05:50.310
First,

103
05:50.510 --> 05:54.460
resolutely oppose the Nationalist government's betrayal of China's sovereignty.

104
05:54.460 --> 05:56.320
Brother Zurong, Brother Zurong.

105
05:56.360 --> 05:57.290
Generalissimo,

106
05:57.510 --> 05:59.700
I believe the Communist army's so-called resistance against Japan

107
05:59.700 --> 06:00.990
is nothing more than a ploy to attract public attention

108
06:00.990 --> 06:01.870
and win domestic

109
06:01.870 --> 06:03.560
and international support,

110
06:03.580 --> 06:05.250
all to tie down our forces.

111
06:05.280 --> 06:06.920
I agree with Commander Chen's judgment.

112
06:06.000 --> 06:09.170
[He Guoguang, Commissioner of Nanchang Headquarters]

113
06:07.230 --> 06:09.420
Based on the information we currently have,

114
06:09.420 --> 06:10.690
they have no intention of leaving

115
06:10.690 --> 06:11.960
the core area of the Communist army.

116
06:11.960 --> 06:13.240
Moreover, they are setting up their formations,

117
06:13.240 --> 06:15.770
preparing for a life-and-death battle with our six columns.

118
06:15.770 --> 06:18.030
The Communist army's combat operations have always been decisive

119
06:18.030 --> 06:19.080
and purposeful.

120
06:19.190 --> 06:20.330
But since last year,

121
06:19.700 --> 06:24.390
[Yang Yongtae, Secretary of Nanchang Headquarters]

122
06:20.360 --> 06:22.130
it has been completely different from before.

123
06:22.130 --> 06:24.520
All their deployments are self-contradictory.

124
06:24.520 --> 06:26.040
It's truly baffling.

125
06:26.070 --> 06:26.920
Gentlemen,

126
06:28.890 --> 06:31.850
I don't think the Communist army is untraceable.

127
06:34.640 --> 06:36.200
That Kong something...

128
06:36.870 --> 06:37.830
Kong Hechong.

129
06:38.090 --> 06:38.980
Call him over.

130
06:46.860 --> 06:48.630
[Chen Cheng, Nationalist Army Commander-in-Chief of the Northern Route Army at the Front and Commander of the Third Route Army]

131
06:53.250 --> 06:54.200
Generalissimo,

132
07:04.560 --> 07:05.560
This Mr. Kong

133
07:06.000 --> 07:09.120
defected from their side.

134
07:08.810 --> 07:11.200
[Kong Hechong Former Commander of the Red 16th Army]

135
07:09.400 --> 07:11.490
He is here to help us formulate a battle plan.

136
07:11.230 --> 07:12.930
[Yan Daogang Director of the Chairman's Attendants' Office, Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

137
07:11.720 --> 07:14.760
He also has some important intelligence on the Communist army.

138
07:14.760 --> 07:15.610
Speak.

139
07:17.650 --> 07:18.530
Mao Zedong

140
07:18.600 --> 07:20.860
has already lost command of the Red Army.

141
07:21.230 --> 07:24.840
The ones currently commanding the Central Red Army against your army...

142
07:24.840 --> 07:26.010
Our army

143
07:26.090 --> 07:28.630
are Qin Bangxian (Bo Gu), who has no military experience,

144
07:28.630 --> 07:30.750
and the German advisor Li De.

145
07:30.900 --> 07:32.159
The "fortress against fortress" tactic

146
07:32.159 --> 07:33.450
is advocated by Li De.

147
07:37.460 --> 07:38.990
Zurong, continue reading.

148
07:39.390 --> 07:40.120
Yes.

149
07:42.040 --> 07:44.690
Oppose recognition of the puppet state of Manchukuo.

150
07:44.690 --> 07:48.090
Second, immediately sever diplomatic relations with Japan

151
07:48.640 --> 07:49.570
and declare all

152
07:49.600 --> 07:53.190
secret treaties and agreements between China and Japan null and void.

153
07:53.190 --> 07:54.670
Mobilize China's

154
07:54.690 --> 07:57.820
army, navy, and air force to fight Japan.

155
07:58.180 --> 08:00.740
Third, arm the people nationwide,

156
08:01.010 --> 08:03.430
and organize volunteer forces and guerrilla units

157
08:03.430 --> 08:05.830
to take an active part in the war of resistance against Japan.

158
08:05.830 --> 08:08.120
Actively support the Northeast Anti-Japanese Volunteer Army

159
08:08.120 --> 08:13.850
and the Northward Anti-Japanese Expeditionary Force of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army.

160
08:19.060 --> 08:23.780
[Lanshan Ridge, Huichang, Jiangxi]

161
08:27.410 --> 08:28.210
Chairman Mao,

162
08:29.240 --> 08:31.290
let's go down the mountain first.

163
08:31.800 --> 08:33.570
Vice Chairman Zhou specifically instructed me

164
08:33.570 --> 08:35.700
to escort you back as soon as possible.

165
08:36.280 --> 08:38.419
We're already halfway up the mountain.

166
08:38.419 --> 08:42.830
[Chen Shijie Commander of the Training Battalion, 1st Red Army Corps]

167
08:38.720 --> 08:40.780
There's no reason to give up halfway.

168
08:41.360 --> 08:43.150
Alright, I'll listen to you.

169
08:44.140 --> 08:44.940
Chen Shiju,

170
08:45.470 --> 08:47.000
if I remember correctly,

171
08:47.240 --> 08:49.360
after the Sanwan Reorganization,

172
08:50.140 --> 08:53.510
when I proposed that party branches should be established at the company level,

173
08:53.510 --> 08:56.160
you were one of the party members whose oath ceremony I presided over.

174
08:56.160 --> 08:58.160
Chairman, you remember correctly.

175
08:58.510 --> 08:59.910
I was in the First Company,

176
08:59.910 --> 09:01.510
and I still clearly remember

177
09:01.530 --> 09:03.120
the party admission oath from back then.

178
09:03.120 --> 09:05.720
Sacrifice the individual. Strive for the revolution.

179
09:05.720 --> 09:08.550
Engage in class struggle. Obey the organization.

180
09:08.960 --> 09:11.890
Strictly maintain secrecy. Never betray the Party.

181
09:12.080 --> 09:13.080
It's been 7 years.

182
09:13.730 --> 09:16.010
Now our company party branches

183
09:16.040 --> 09:18.500
have spread throughout the entire Red Army.

184
09:19.050 --> 09:21.050
Chairman Mao, I still remember

185
09:21.410 --> 09:23.670
what you looked like when I first met you.

186
09:23.750 --> 09:24.510
Tell me.

187
09:25.000 --> 09:26.670
It was during the Autumn Harvest Uprising.

188
09:26.670 --> 09:27.840
For a few days,

189
09:28.010 --> 09:29.210
I saw a tall man

190
09:29.600 --> 09:30.870
in our First Company's ranks,

191
09:30.870 --> 09:31.810
carrying a load on a shoulder pole,

192
09:31.810 --> 09:34.170
walking back and forth.

193
09:34.390 --> 09:35.660
I thought he was a porter,

194
09:35.660 --> 09:37.720
so I called him over to carry our load.

195
09:37.850 --> 09:38.910
This tall man said:

196
09:39.450 --> 09:40.980
"I've been carrying water for 3 days.

197
09:40.980 --> 09:42.710
Today the Company let me rest."

198
09:42.920 --> 09:44.320
Later, the Company Commander told me

199
09:44.320 --> 09:46.250
that the tall man was you.

200
09:49.130 --> 09:50.100
That tall man.

201
09:52.870 --> 09:55.730
I really can't remember what you're talking about.

202
09:55.870 --> 09:57.960
But I am that tall man.

203
10:14.330 --> 10:16.600
Chairman Mao, let's eat something here.

204
10:17.430 --> 10:18.030
Okay.

205
10:18.310 --> 10:19.350
Come, come.

206
10:33.530 --> 10:34.790
Come, you two eat some.

207
10:34.840 --> 10:35.840
Thank you, Chief.

208
10:48.400 --> 10:49.520
Dawn is breaking;

209
10:51.110 --> 10:52.740
never think you're up early.

210
10:53.780 --> 10:55.270
Never think you're up early.

211
10:55.270 --> 10:56.630
For there are always others up earlier.

212
10:56.630 --> 10:57.960
That's a good comeback.

213
10:58.880 --> 11:00.550
Never think you're up early.

214
11:01.100 --> 11:03.560
There are always others already on the road.

215
11:05.520 --> 11:07.210
Are you trying to compose a poem with me?

216
11:07.210 --> 11:09.070
Chairman Mao, I'm no good at that.

217
11:12.490 --> 11:15.140
This is not a poem; it's a ci.

218
11:19.150 --> 11:20.270
Dawn is breaking;

219
11:21.880 --> 11:23.480
Never think you're up early.

220
11:24.970 --> 11:27.570
I've crossed green mountains, yet I'm not old.

221
11:28.560 --> 11:31.730
The scenery here is the finest of all.

222
11:49.360 --> 11:51.750
Beyond Huichang City, lofty peaks

223
11:53.270 --> 11:56.070
stretch one after another toward the eastern sea.

224
11:58.380 --> 12:01.040
The soldiers point toward southern Guangdong,

225
12:02.900 --> 12:06.260
where the hills grow ever more lush and green.

226
12:22.730 --> 12:25.780
On July 23, 1934,

227
12:25.780 --> 12:27.180
the Central Secretariat of the Communist Party of China

228
12:27.180 --> 12:29.260
and the Central Revolutionary Military Commission issued

229
12:29.260 --> 12:30.780
the Directive on the Transfer

230
12:30.780 --> 12:32.490
of the Red 6th Army Corps to Central Hunan,

231
12:32.490 --> 12:36.420
addressed to the Red 6th Army Corps and the Hunan-Jiangxi Military District.

232
12:36.420 --> 12:37.690
The directive laid out detailed plans

233
12:37.690 --> 12:39.300
and arrangements for the Red 6th Army Corps

234
12:39.300 --> 12:42.330
to leave the Hunan-Jiangxi Soviet Area

235
12:42.330 --> 12:44.830
and establish a new revolutionary base in Hunan.

236
12:44.830 --> 12:46.860
Upon receiving the order, the Red 6th Army Corps

237
12:46.860 --> 12:48.340
urgently mobilized

238
12:48.360 --> 12:51.790
and assembled its main force, including the 17th and 18th Divisions,

239
12:51.790 --> 12:53.820
together with teachers and students from the Hunan-Jiangxi Red Army School,

240
12:53.820 --> 12:55.820
totaling more than 9,700 people.

241
12:56.040 --> 12:57.210
On August 7,

242
12:57.570 --> 13:01.140
they set out on their westward expedition

243
13:01.220 --> 13:05.080
from Hengshi and Xinjiangkou in Suichuan County, Jiangxi Province.

244
13:07.380 --> 13:08.330
Comrades!

245
13:09.300 --> 13:12.160
We are about to leave the Hunan-Jiangxi Soviet Area

246
13:12.570 --> 13:14.300
and begin our long expedition!

247
13:14.900 --> 13:15.810
Like all of you,

248
13:16.180 --> 13:18.770
I'm reluctant to leave this place behind.

249
13:18.630 --> 13:21.900
[Ren Bishi Representative of the CPC Central Committee Chairman of the Military and Political Commission of the Red 6th Army Corps]

250
13:19.900 --> 13:23.020
I am reluctant to leave the base area we personally created,

251
13:23.020 --> 13:25.490
every mountain, every river,

252
13:25.940 --> 13:27.850
every blade of grass, and every tree here.

253
13:27.850 --> 13:29.470
What I am most reluctant to leave

254
13:29.470 --> 13:31.400
are the elders, fellow villagers,

255
13:31.810 --> 13:34.690
relatives, and comrades-in-arms of the base area.

256
13:35.530 --> 13:36.980
But an order is an order.

257
13:37.420 --> 13:40.380
The Party's instructions are above all else.

258
13:40.580 --> 13:41.490
Even with all our reluctance,

259
13:41.490 --> 13:43.620
we still have to embark on the journey.

260
13:43.690 --> 13:45.660
Comrades, this journey

261
13:45.940 --> 13:48.490
will surely be across thousands of mountains and rivers.

262
13:48.490 --> 13:50.900
We may face a perilous path fraught with danger.

263
13:50.900 --> 13:51.960
We don't know when,

264
13:52.330 --> 13:54.140
or even if, we'll return.

265
13:55.570 --> 13:58.330
So here, let us bid farewell

266
13:58.490 --> 14:00.850
with a soldier's salute— to these mountains and rivers,

267
14:00.850 --> 14:04.540
every tree and blade of grass, and to the local people,

268
14:05.210 --> 14:07.010
our families, and our comrades.

269
14:07.900 --> 14:08.940
Salute!

270
14:09.760 --> 14:11.010
[Li Da, Chief of Staff of the Red 6th Army Corps]

271
14:25.100 --> 14:26.870
[Xiao Ke Commander of the Red 6th Army Corps]

272
14:26.950 --> 14:28.500
[Wang Zhen Political Commissar of the Red 6th Army Corps]

273
14:29.920 --> 14:31.540
[Zhang Ziyi Director of the Political Department of the Red 6th Army Corps]

274
14:38.020 --> 14:38.660
Move out!

275
14:38.690 --> 14:39.940
Left turn!

276
14:41.000 --> 14:42.090
Forward march!

277
14:46.210 --> 14:47.450
Right turn!

278
14:48.570 --> 14:49.850
Forward march!

279
14:51.900 --> 14:53.100
Listen to my command!

280
14:53.180 --> 14:54.260
Forward march!

281
14:57.330 --> 14:58.570
Right turn!

282
14:59.690 --> 15:00.550
Forward march!

283
15:20.120 --> 15:23.230
[Chen Congying Cadre of the Confidential Communications Section of the Hunan-Jiangxi Provincial Party Committee and Wife of Ren Bishi]

284
15:48.780 --> 15:49.990
It's time to go.

285
16:49.540 --> 16:51.790
After the founding of the People's Republic of China,

286
16:51.790 --> 16:52.930
Ren Bishi and his wife

287
16:52.930 --> 16:56.150
searched far and wide for Little Xianggan's whereabouts,

288
16:56.150 --> 16:58.080
but ultimately failed to find him.

289
17:00.210 --> 17:03.020
Starting in August 1934,

290
17:03.970 --> 17:06.050
the Kuomintang army under Chen Cheng,

291
17:06.050 --> 17:07.710
with a force of six divisions,

292
17:08.010 --> 17:09.730
under the cover of dozens of planes

293
17:09.730 --> 17:12.579
and hundreds of new mountain guns,

294
17:13.030 --> 17:16.490
launched a general offensive against the Red Army positions.

295
17:17.140 --> 17:18.780
The Red Army's fortress fortifications

296
17:18.780 --> 17:20.670
were unable to effectively block the enemy.

297
17:20.670 --> 17:22.730
The Red Army suffered heavy casualties

298
17:22.730 --> 17:24.480
and was forced to retreat to Yiqian

299
17:24.480 --> 17:26.940
to continue to block the enemy's offensive.

300
17:27.810 --> 17:30.500
The eastern and northern fronts of the Central Soviet Area

301
17:30.500 --> 17:34.100
faced the danger of being broken through by the enemy at any time.

302
17:34.530 --> 17:37.140
The situation on the western and southern fronts

303
17:37.140 --> 17:39.000
was also increasingly critical.

304
17:43.150 --> 17:46.380
[Yunshi Mountain, Ruijin, Jiangxi]

305
17:45.470 --> 17:46.340
Chairman Mao,

306
17:46.690 --> 17:48.310
this is the residence arranged by the Central Committee

307
17:48.310 --> 17:49.420
for you and Comrade Luofu.

308
17:49.420 --> 17:51.710
Vice Chairman Zhou said it's quiet in this temple,

309
17:51.710 --> 17:53.450
convenient for you to read and write.

310
17:53.450 --> 17:55.050
Enlai is really thoughtful.

311
17:55.660 --> 17:56.790
Has Luofu moved in?

312
17:57.530 --> 17:58.710
He went to inspect the Fujian-Jiangxi Province

313
17:58.710 --> 18:00.110
and hasn't returned yet.

314
18:04.420 --> 18:05.420
In Jinggangshan,

315
18:05.690 --> 18:07.290
I lived in Xiangshan Nunnery

316
18:07.490 --> 18:09.550
and Baiyun Temple in Buyun Mountain.

317
18:09.690 --> 18:13.530
Two years ago, I went to the ancient temple in Donghua Mountain to recuperate.

318
18:13.530 --> 18:16.150
Now I've moved into this Yunshan Ancient Temple.

319
18:16.150 --> 18:17.680
It seems that I, Mao Zedong,

320
18:17.940 --> 18:20.740
really have some affinity with monks and Buddhas.

321
18:20.940 --> 18:23.270
What do you think of the environment here?

322
18:29.590 --> 18:35.040
Clouds welcome the Buddha; this place is no less sacred than the land of India.

323
18:37.970 --> 18:42.780
Stones hone one's true nature; how many can walk straight to the flower seller?

324
18:44.690 --> 18:46.750
This couplet is a bit awkward to read.

325
18:46.820 --> 18:47.820
What does it mean?

326
18:50.450 --> 18:51.310
Hurry up and go.

327
18:52.940 --> 18:54.010
Amitabha.

328
18:54.900 --> 18:56.940
How should I address you, Master?

329
18:57.010 --> 18:58.900
I am Luo Neng.

330
18:57.790 --> 19:00.150
[Luo Neng, Abbot of Yunshan Temple]

331
18:59.420 --> 19:01.820
Master Luoneng, may I ask

332
19:02.490 --> 19:04.660
what this couplet means?

333
19:04.490 --> 19:05.810
[He Zizhen, Mao Zedong's wife]

334
19:06.520 --> 19:08.590
It's an acrostic couplet.

335
19:08.820 --> 19:12.340
The first characters of the two lines together form

336
19:12.580 --> 19:13.580
"Yunshi,"

337
19:13.940 --> 19:17.940
matching the name of the mountain where this ancient temple is located.

338
19:17.940 --> 19:19.140
The first line means

339
19:19.290 --> 19:21.860
this is an ideal place for spiritual cultivation.

340
19:21.860 --> 19:25.380
The second says that spiritual practice

341
19:25.620 --> 19:28.210
requires not only the tempering of one's mind and character,

342
19:28.210 --> 19:30.610
but also alludes to a historical anecdote.

343
19:31.340 --> 19:32.250
What anecdote?

344
19:32.660 --> 19:34.770
The Sutra of a Hundred Conditions tells the story

345
19:34.770 --> 19:36.530
of a flower seller

346
19:36.580 --> 19:38.780
who was selling a bouquet at the market.

347
19:38.940 --> 19:40.100
Two people came along,

348
19:40.100 --> 19:43.250
and both wanted to buy the flowers to offer to the Buddha.

349
19:43.450 --> 19:45.530
They kept outbidding each other

350
19:45.770 --> 19:48.940
until the price reached a hundred thousand gold coins.

351
19:49.450 --> 19:51.620
Then the flower seller said

352
19:51.900 --> 19:52.890
he would no longer sell the flowers.

353
19:52.890 --> 19:55.290
He would offer them to the Buddha himself

354
19:55.540 --> 19:57.780
and cultivate his own merit.

355
19:59.660 --> 20:01.180
Cultivate his own merit?

356
20:01.730 --> 20:03.730
That shows he had attained enlightenment.

357
20:03.730 --> 20:04.860
What did he realize?

358
20:05.730 --> 20:08.060
The Buddha can be worshipped by everyone,

359
20:08.140 --> 20:11.340
but each person must recite the scriptures for themselves.

360
20:11.340 --> 20:14.290
To explain such a complicated allusion

361
20:14.380 --> 20:16.660
in such simple terms—

362
20:17.210 --> 20:19.490
that's what makes someone a truly enlightened master.

363
20:19.490 --> 20:22.090
It's just a matter of different perspectives.

364
20:22.340 --> 20:23.290
Master Luoneng,

365
20:23.530 --> 20:26.210
where are you going?

366
20:27.180 --> 20:29.820
I am looking for another place to live.

367
20:30.290 --> 20:31.010
Why?

368
20:31.100 --> 20:31.900
Chairman Mao,

369
20:32.600 --> 20:33.290
we were concerned for

370
20:33.290 --> 20:34.730
the safety of you and Comrade Luofu,

371
20:34.730 --> 20:35.660
so he...

372
20:37.280 --> 20:39.210
We're disturbing his spiritual practice,

373
20:39.210 --> 20:41.070
yet you're asking him to move out?

374
20:41.210 --> 20:42.340
That's outrageous.

375
20:43.250 --> 20:44.180
Master Luoneng,

376
20:45.100 --> 20:46.420
we're the ones imposing on you.

377
20:46.420 --> 20:47.480
Don't go anywhere.

378
20:47.620 --> 20:48.450
Just stay here

379
20:49.320 --> 20:49.840
I...

380
20:49.870 --> 20:50.790
Just stay here.

381
20:51.380 --> 20:52.780
Don't hesitate anymore.

382
20:52.900 --> 20:54.300
Take it as an expedient means,

383
20:54.300 --> 20:56.630
unless you want to return to secular life.

384
20:57.170 --> 20:58.450
Well said. Well said.

385
20:58.480 --> 20:59.680
Well said. Well said.

386
21:00.580 --> 21:01.130
Chairman.

387
21:01.130 --> 21:02.060
Go back quickly.

388
21:02.140 --> 21:03.420
You stay in this room.

389
21:04.830 --> 21:07.380
You two have a fine assignment.

390
21:08.290 --> 21:09.530
Set up my desk

391
21:09.970 --> 21:11.690
and prepare the Four Treasures of the Study.

392
21:11.690 --> 21:12.970
Enlai asked me to write

393
21:13.050 --> 21:14.730
a little booklet on guerrilla warfare.

394
21:14.730 --> 21:16.150
I haven't finished the ending yet.

395
21:16.150 --> 21:16.760
Yes.

396
21:17.290 --> 21:19.620
Wasn't that choice assignment supposed to be mine?

397
21:19.620 --> 21:21.950
Your assignment is to grind the ink for me.

398
21:23.100 --> 21:24.530
But before that choice assignment,

399
21:24.530 --> 21:25.800
could you take on a tough one?

400
21:25.800 --> 21:26.560
Go ahead.

401
21:26.780 --> 21:28.820
Cook, and then pick up Maomao.

402
21:29.490 --> 21:31.290
I'd better pick up Maomao first.

403
21:37.520 --> 21:42.490
[Shicheng Front Line, Ganzhou, Jiangxi]

404
21:43.380 --> 21:45.770
Peng, there's an urgent telegram from the Military Commission.

405
21:45.770 --> 21:46.860
Just tell me the main points.

406
21:46.860 --> 21:47.860
The telegram says

407
21:48.140 --> 21:49.490
we must adopt mobile defense

408
21:49.490 --> 21:50.750
as our basic operational principle

409
21:50.750 --> 21:53.810
[Deng Ping, Chief of Staff of 3rd Red Army Corps]

410
21:51.140 --> 21:52.770
and keep the enemy north of Shicheng.

411
21:52.770 --> 21:54.210
In carrying out this mission,

412
21:53.810 --> 21:56.910
[Yang Shangkun Political Commissar of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

413
21:54.290 --> 21:55.580
we must conserve our manpower and material resources

414
21:55.580 --> 21:57.940
to the greatest extent possible,

415
21:58.380 --> 22:01.340
then use lulls between battles to replenish and retrain our troops.

416
21:59.600 --> 22:01.850
[Peng Dehuai Commander of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

417
22:01.510 --> 22:04.770
We must also strengthen political unity within the ranks.

418
22:05.290 --> 22:07.400
Looks like these foreign advisers are finally catching on?

419
22:07.400 --> 22:10.130
Look, the telegram is signed only by Zhu and Zhou.

420
22:10.410 --> 22:11.580
There's no Li or Bo.

421
22:13.030 --> 22:14.030
No wonder.

422
22:14.190 --> 22:16.450
Those foreign advisers are out of ideas.

423
22:17.420 --> 22:20.100
We still have to rely on Commander-in-Chief Zhu and Comrade Enlai.

424
22:20.100 --> 22:21.290
If we'd fought this way from the start,

425
22:21.290 --> 22:23.070
how many comrades could we have spared?

426
22:23.070 --> 22:23.830
Exactly.

427
22:27.490 --> 22:29.690
If we'd followed Mao's earlier approach,

428
22:29.690 --> 22:31.650
we wouldn't have ended up in this situation.

429
22:31.650 --> 22:34.050
Then let's pass on the orders accordingly.

430
23:02.020 --> 23:04.740
Runzhi, your footbath is ready.

431
23:19.820 --> 23:21.410
Aren't you going to test the water temperature?

432
23:21.410 --> 23:23.210
You must have tested it already.

433
23:29.690 --> 23:30.380
Maomao.

434
23:31.690 --> 23:34.730
Maomao, come, soak your feet with me.

435
23:34.730 --> 23:35.940
Soak feet.

436
23:36.210 --> 23:37.100
Is it hot?

437
23:37.730 --> 23:39.380
Come, splash water with me.

438
23:40.250 --> 23:41.690
He's not wearing shoes. His feet are dirty.

439
23:41.690 --> 23:42.490
Splash again.

440
23:42.860 --> 23:43.530
Soak feet.

441
23:43.530 --> 23:45.140
Stop splashing. The water is coming out.

442
23:45.140 --> 23:45.690
You splash.

443
23:45.690 --> 23:47.090
Splash, splash, splash.

444
23:47.140 --> 23:47.450
Come, come, come.

445
23:47.450 --> 23:47.910
Maomao.

446
23:48.530 --> 23:48.970
Together.

447
23:48.970 --> 23:50.030
What are you doing?

448
23:50.490 --> 23:51.100
Together.

449
23:52.450 --> 23:53.900
I... I won't wash.

450
23:54.860 --> 23:56.320
Together with Mom and Dad.

451
23:59.500 --> 24:00.420
Soak feet.

452
24:00.450 --> 24:04.340
Soak feet.

453
24:05.410 --> 24:07.940
I told you to splash water, not step on my feet.

454
24:12.400 --> 24:13.180
Where are you going?

455
24:13.180 --> 24:14.780
Didn't you just wash your feet for nothing?

456
24:14.780 --> 24:15.840
Where are you going?

457
24:15.840 --> 24:16.720
Go out to play.

458
24:21.460 --> 24:23.190
Zizhen, is there any food left?

459
24:23.490 --> 24:24.010
Yes.

460
24:24.010 --> 24:24.580
Luofu,

461
24:25.450 --> 24:26.250
just got back?

462
24:27.180 --> 24:28.040
Have you eaten?

463
24:28.390 --> 24:29.070
Not yet.

464
24:29.100 --> 24:30.500
Then have dinner with us.

465
24:30.630 --> 24:31.360
No.

466
24:31.690 --> 24:34.210
I don't want to disturb your family time.

467
24:34.230 --> 24:37.190
Are you despising my leftovers?

468
24:37.090 --> 24:41.750
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian) Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Central Political Bureau Chairman of the People's Committee of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

469
24:38.900 --> 24:40.160
Then I won't be polite.

470
24:40.590 --> 24:41.850
I'm really hungry.

471
24:42.450 --> 24:43.820
Uncle is hungry.

472
24:46.220 --> 24:46.980
Is it good?

473
24:48.570 --> 24:49.200
It's good.

474
24:49.220 --> 24:50.340
Eat more if it's good.

475
24:50.340 --> 24:51.010
Okay.

476
24:53.050 --> 24:54.940
How was your trip to Fujian-Jiangxi Province?

477
24:54.940 --> 24:56.340
What did you gain from it?

478
24:57.450 --> 24:58.940
It's hard to put into words.

479
24:58.940 --> 25:01.670
I only know how hard it is when I'm in the position.

480
25:01.970 --> 25:03.970
Only after becoming Chairman of the People's Committee

481
25:03.970 --> 25:06.830
did I realize how hard things must have been for you.

482
25:07.100 --> 25:07.940
You're right.

483
25:08.140 --> 25:09.660
You can't handle grassroots work

484
25:09.660 --> 25:12.860
by just reading from a book and following it word for word.

485
25:16.210 --> 25:19.140
Theory must be put into practice.

486
25:21.330 --> 25:24.810
I deeply understand that now.

487
25:26.780 --> 25:27.710
Maomao, Maomao.

488
25:28.340 --> 25:28.970
It's cold.

489
25:31.410 --> 25:34.260
Comrade Zizhen not only cooks well,

490
25:34.620 --> 25:36.750
but also has a wonderfully hearty laugh.

491
25:36.750 --> 25:38.620
You're too kind, Luofu.

492
25:40.790 --> 25:43.650
Luofu, you're thirty-something this year, right?

493
25:44.580 --> 25:46.290
I was born in the Year of the Rat.

494
25:46.290 --> 25:47.890
I'm 35 by Chinese reckoning.

495
25:49.340 --> 25:51.000
Then it's time to get married.

496
25:52.210 --> 25:55.580
I've been alone for so many years. I'm used to it.

497
25:55.730 --> 25:58.970
Besides, the current situation doesn't allow it.

498
26:01.660 --> 26:03.120
I never imagined that you,

499
26:03.940 --> 26:06.380
the pioneer of

500
26:06.380 --> 26:07.940
revolutionary romance novels,

501
26:07.940 --> 26:11.210
would live like the hero of your own story—

502
26:11.290 --> 26:13.490
choosing revolution over love.

503
26:14.580 --> 26:17.820
You've read my novel "Journey?"

504
26:17.840 --> 26:20.670
I had the honor to read it and was deeply moved.

505
26:21.180 --> 26:22.110
Tell me about it.

506
26:23.050 --> 26:25.380
I think the novel "Journey"

507
26:25.490 --> 26:27.600
is different from other literary works

508
26:27.600 --> 26:29.400
by overseas students,

509
26:29.430 --> 26:30.890
which often adopt the posture

510
26:30.890 --> 26:32.550
of citizens of a weak country.

511
26:33.100 --> 26:35.100
Instead, it uses a romantic way

512
26:35.380 --> 26:37.250
to express the enthusiasm for the revolution

513
26:37.250 --> 26:39.450
and the determination to dedicate oneself to it.

514
26:39.450 --> 26:40.610
Don't just praise me.

515
26:40.610 --> 26:41.860
Tell me the shortcomings.

516
26:41.860 --> 26:43.060
The only shortcoming

517
26:43.340 --> 26:44.870
is the ending of your novel.

518
26:45.180 --> 26:47.240
You have the heroine take her own life

519
26:47.250 --> 26:49.290
and the hero sacrifice himself for the revolution.

520
26:49.290 --> 26:50.380
They both die,

521
26:51.690 --> 26:53.950
leaving the reader deeply unsatisfied.

522
26:54.340 --> 26:55.210
In my opinion,

523
26:55.380 --> 26:58.290
the cruelty of revolution and romantic ideals

524
26:58.420 --> 27:00.620
don't need to be completely separated.

525
27:01.010 --> 27:04.970
Even the revolution itself is full of romanticism.

526
27:07.140 --> 27:08.100
Comrade Zedong,

527
27:08.120 --> 27:11.120
you are really a unique person.

528
27:11.620 --> 27:14.820
You're so practical when it comes to revolution and getting things done,

529
27:14.820 --> 27:16.900
yet so romantic

530
27:17.290 --> 27:18.660
when discussing literature and writing poetry.

531
27:18.660 --> 27:21.820
I heard you wrote a poem

532
27:22.250 --> 27:23.710
in Huichang a few days ago,

533
27:23.900 --> 27:28.140
titled "The Scenery Here Is Uniquely Beautiful."

534
27:30.380 --> 27:33.980
The revolutionary cause will always have its own unique beauty.

535
27:41.260 --> 27:45.090
Luofu, you've given me a whole new impression of you today.

536
27:45.730 --> 27:47.260
I didn't expect that one day

537
27:47.620 --> 27:49.420
we'd sit down and talk like this,

538
27:49.770 --> 27:51.620
let alone find so much to agree on.

539
27:51.620 --> 27:52.340
Yes.

540
27:54.010 --> 27:55.740
We should thank Enlai for this.

541
27:55.860 --> 27:57.860
He arranged for us to live together.

542
27:58.130 --> 27:59.170
Comrade Zedong,

543
27:59.490 --> 28:03.770
in the past, I always felt that you were too domineering.

544
28:04.380 --> 28:07.100
So some people said you were a mountain king,

545
28:07.180 --> 28:09.490
making people keep a respectful distance.

546
28:09.490 --> 28:11.450
But after our chat today,

547
28:11.820 --> 28:14.530
I see you in a completely new light.

548
28:15.040 --> 28:20.080
I feel I should respect and get close to you.

549
28:22.500 --> 28:24.650
Of course, what I agree with

550
28:24.840 --> 28:26.190
is not only your poetry,

551
28:26.410 --> 28:30.300
but also your pragmatic policy propositions.

552
28:31.340 --> 28:34.610
Do you know what inspired me

553
28:35.170 --> 28:37.830
during my trip to Fujian and Jiangxi provinces?

554
28:39.010 --> 28:40.410
Please tell me in detail.

555
28:40.490 --> 28:41.450
Last month,

556
28:41.660 --> 28:42.880
I happened to see

557
28:43.100 --> 28:45.660
an article you wrote in 1930.

558
28:45.970 --> 28:48.180
It says:

559
28:52.820 --> 28:54.140
Step out

560
28:54.340 --> 28:56.210
and go to all parts and places

561
28:56.580 --> 28:59.010
within your scope of work.

562
28:59.450 --> 29:01.840
Learn from Confucius to ask about everything.

563
29:01.840 --> 29:03.580
No matter how limited your abilities may be,

564
29:03.580 --> 29:05.240
you can still solve problems.

565
29:05.640 --> 29:08.490
Before you leave, your mind is empty.

566
29:09.100 --> 29:11.970
When you return, it is no longer empty.

567
29:12.530 --> 29:13.690
You've gathered

568
29:13.900 --> 29:17.450
all the information needed to solve the problems.

569
29:17.490 --> 29:21.580
That's how problems are solved.

570
29:21.660 --> 29:24.180
Luofu, this is my article

571
29:24.660 --> 29:25.990
"Oppose Book Worship".

572
29:26.100 --> 29:26.900
Yes.

573
29:27.660 --> 29:30.320
I never thought anyone would find that article,

574
29:31.660 --> 29:32.770
let alone read it.

575
29:33.660 --> 29:35.390
And you even took notes from it.

576
29:36.180 --> 29:38.690
That's truly something.

577
29:39.320 --> 29:43.050
It was only after taking over as Chairman of the People's Committee

578
29:43.390 --> 29:47.630
that I realized how hard it is to get anything done.

579
29:48.610 --> 29:50.130
I was slow to see it.

580
29:52.660 --> 29:53.660
Luofu,

581
29:54.100 --> 29:57.250
I've actually been paying attention to you too.

582
29:57.590 --> 29:58.520
In June,

583
29:58.900 --> 29:59.860
I saw

584
30:00.050 --> 30:02.100
the article you published in "Struggle",

585
30:02.100 --> 30:05.300
"Opposing the Ultra-Leftism of the Petty Bourgeoisie".

586
30:06.010 --> 30:07.880
You argued that ultra-leftism

587
30:07.900 --> 30:10.420
is another form of opportunism.

588
30:10.650 --> 30:12.050
That's very insightful.

589
30:12.860 --> 30:14.390
I have a lot to be ashamed of.

590
30:14.540 --> 30:17.500
After studying Marxism for so many years,

591
30:17.620 --> 30:21.290
I still found myself comfortably ensconced in

592
30:21.340 --> 30:22.600
the camp of "leftism."

593
30:23.540 --> 30:26.170
I need to be more vigilant in the future.

594
30:28.030 --> 30:29.430
Yiqian has fallen.

595
30:30.300 --> 30:32.970
The situation is unfolding just as you predicted.

596
30:32.970 --> 30:36.500
Our defenses are wide open, and the Soviet Area may soon be lost.

597
30:37.470 --> 30:40.270
I am deeply worried.

598
30:41.600 --> 30:43.680
I don't know what you think.

599
30:54.010 --> 30:55.410
I'm on the sidelines now.

600
30:56.420 --> 30:57.620
They won't listen to

601
30:58.530 --> 30:59.970
anything I say.

602
31:00.620 --> 31:02.660
You still have to say what needs to be said.

603
31:02.660 --> 31:03.490
Naturally.

604
31:03.940 --> 31:04.820
But Luofu,

605
31:05.180 --> 31:07.140
my words alone won't be enough.

606
31:07.420 --> 31:10.490
I can't just make claims without solid backing.

607
31:11.770 --> 31:13.690
I've already told Enlai.

608
31:13.970 --> 31:17.030
I'll leave the mountain first thing tomorrow morning.

609
31:17.380 --> 31:18.340
I'll walk around

610
31:19.690 --> 31:22.210
and learn from Confucius to ask about everything.

611
31:22.210 --> 31:23.810
Didn't I say in that article,

612
31:24.020 --> 31:27.020
"Without investigation, you have no right to speak."

613
31:28.350 --> 31:29.480
Where are you going?

614
31:30.940 --> 31:31.860
Yudu,

615
31:33.010 --> 31:34.210
in southern Jiangxi.

616
31:36.940 --> 31:38.210
I'm going to the restroom.

617
31:38.210 --> 31:39.250
We'll talk later.

618
31:39.530 --> 31:40.240
Okay.

619
32:01.580 --> 32:02.580
Remember,

620
32:02.600 --> 32:06.400
don't lose your temper, don't bang the table, and don't stay up late.

621
32:06.580 --> 32:07.710
Get some rest.

622
32:12.600 --> 32:13.660
What are you doing?

623
32:13.900 --> 32:14.880
Reporting to Chairman Mao,

624
32:14.880 --> 32:17.100
we were sent by the General Affairs Office of the Central Government

625
32:17.100 --> 32:18.970
to go to Yudu with you.

626
32:19.400 --> 32:20.530
I arranged for them.

627
32:21.490 --> 32:22.420
Comrade Zedong,

628
32:22.770 --> 32:25.690
your trip to Yudu this time carries heavy responsibilities.

629
32:25.690 --> 32:27.140
It's close to the enemy-occupied area,

630
32:27.140 --> 32:28.580
and the situation is quite complicated.

631
32:28.580 --> 32:30.620
The General Affairs Office has the responsibility

632
32:30.620 --> 32:32.350
to ensure your work and safety.

633
32:33.140 --> 32:34.470
His name is Hu Changbao.

634
32:34.580 --> 32:36.770
He is a veteran from the communication platoon

635
32:36.770 --> 32:38.270
and is very responsible in his work.

636
32:38.270 --> 32:41.580
From now on, let him be your guard squad leader.

637
32:42.380 --> 32:43.250
Comrade Luofu,

638
32:43.270 --> 32:46.420
I haven't enjoyed such treatment for a long time.

639
32:46.650 --> 32:47.850
I'm deeply grateful.

640
32:48.850 --> 32:51.770
Our conversation last night left me wanting more.

641
32:52.490 --> 32:56.180
Let's have a good talk when you come back.

642
32:56.290 --> 32:56.900
Okay.

643
32:57.050 --> 32:57.620
Squad Leader Hu!

644
32:57.620 --> 32:58.140
Here!

645
32:58.380 --> 33:00.580
Make sure Chairman Mao stays safe.

646
33:00.690 --> 33:02.220
I'll carry out the mission!

647
33:05.960 --> 33:07.970
Chairman Mao hasn't been feeling well lately.

648
33:07.970 --> 33:10.490
You two young comrades must take good care of him.

649
33:10.490 --> 33:11.620
Report to me immediately

650
33:11.620 --> 33:13.180
if anything happens.

651
33:14.210 --> 33:15.620
We'll carry out the mission!

652
33:15.620 --> 33:18.100
How do you know I haven't been feeling well lately?

653
33:18.100 --> 33:20.630
You kept coughing during our chat last night.

654
33:24.010 --> 33:25.530
Goodbye, Comrade Luofu.

655
33:25.770 --> 33:26.580
Goodbye.

656
33:30.900 --> 33:32.300
Your name is Hu Changbao?

657
33:32.370 --> 33:34.170
Reporting to the Chairman, yes.

658
33:34.340 --> 33:37.010
Then you must protect me for a long time.

659
33:37.530 --> 33:38.100
Yes.

660
33:38.830 --> 33:41.040
I'll protect you for a long time.

661
33:59.140 --> 34:00.180
Comrades of the Red Army.

662
34:00.180 --> 34:00.580
Hello, fellow villager.

663
34:00.580 --> 34:02.580
Hello, Chief.

664
34:03.090 --> 34:03.690
Thank you, Chief.

665
34:03.690 --> 34:04.180
It's nothing.

666
34:04.180 --> 34:05.530
Go. Be careful.

667
34:05.580 --> 34:06.580
Okay, Chief.

668
34:13.699 --> 34:14.500
Hello, Chief.

669
34:15.090 --> 34:16.489
Vice Chairman Zhou.

670
34:16.489 --> 34:17.420
What are you making?

671
34:17.420 --> 34:18.170
These are rice cakes.

672
34:18.170 --> 34:19.370
Let me give you a hand.

673
34:20.610 --> 34:21.810
They look delicious!

674
34:24.179 --> 34:24.860
Come on.

675
34:25.010 --> 34:25.810
Hello, Chief.

676
34:26.300 --> 34:28.130
If you join the army, join the Red Army;

677
34:28.130 --> 34:30.730
Workers and peasants welcome you everywhere.

678
34:35.570 --> 34:36.230
Be careful.

679
34:36.239 --> 34:37.040
Give me a hand.

680
34:37.820 --> 34:38.750
Watch your step!

681
34:40.420 --> 34:40.900
Come on.

682
34:42.900 --> 34:43.560
Be careful.

683
34:43.739 --> 34:45.130
It's okay.

684
34:50.489 --> 34:51.530
Okay, let's go.

685
34:52.070 --> 34:53.320
Thank you.

686
34:53.630 --> 34:55.590
Comrades, good news.

687
34:56.360 --> 34:58.920
Comrade Bo Gu, what's your good news?

688
34:59.340 --> 35:00.130
Take a look.

689
35:00.820 --> 35:05.090
The Comintern has sent its reply.

690
35:05.090 --> 35:07.780
It has, in principle, approved

691
35:07.780 --> 35:11.260
the Central Secretariat's plan

692
35:11.260 --> 35:15.700
for the main force of the Red Army to withdraw from the base areas

693
35:15.700 --> 35:22.130
and make a strategic shift toward Hunan.

694
35:22.740 --> 35:23.700
It now seems

695
35:23.720 --> 35:24.860
that our original plan is feasible:

696
35:24.590 --> 35:27.140
[Xiang Ying, Secretary of the Central Secretariat; Vice Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

697
35:24.880 --> 35:27.390
break through the line

698
35:27.490 --> 35:28.450
between Xinfeng and Anyuan,

699
35:28.450 --> 35:30.700
then advance toward Hunan.

700
35:32.220 --> 35:33.080
Comrade Enlai,

701
35:33.650 --> 35:35.300
how are the negotiations

702
35:35.300 --> 35:36.300
with Chen Jitang's forces going?

703
35:36.300 --> 35:37.010
I've already arranged

704
35:37.010 --> 35:39.080
for Comrades Pan Hannian and He Changgong

705
35:39.080 --> 35:40.890
to open talks with the Guangdong Army.

706
35:40.890 --> 35:41.730
We need to hurry.

707
35:41.730 --> 35:43.860
Under our existing operational plan,

708
35:43.970 --> 35:45.130
Yudu is

709
35:45.860 --> 35:46.970
the best and most suitable place

710
35:46.970 --> 35:49.100
for the troops to assemble and set out.

711
35:49.490 --> 35:50.880
Should we send someone to Yudu

712
35:50.880 --> 35:53.340
to investigate the situation on the ground?

713
35:53.530 --> 35:54.190
Comrade Mao Zedong

714
35:54.190 --> 35:56.650
has already started investigating in Yudu.

715
35:56.740 --> 35:58.800
Comrade Mao Zedong is already there?

716
36:01.490 --> 36:02.170
Does Comrade Mao Zedong

717
36:02.170 --> 36:03.450
know about our relocation plan?

718
36:03.450 --> 36:04.380
He doesn't know.

719
36:04.860 --> 36:06.740
Today, when I assigned Comrade He Changgong

720
36:06.740 --> 36:08.170
to handle the negotiations,

721
36:08.170 --> 36:08.970
he told me

722
36:08.970 --> 36:11.110
that Zedong had been investigating in Huichang.

723
36:11.110 --> 36:14.220
He repeatedly stressed the need to resume the tungsten trade

724
36:14.220 --> 36:17.010
and maintain contact with Chen Jitang.

725
36:17.130 --> 36:20.610
He said it could solve major problems when necessary.

726
36:22.450 --> 36:24.530
He is always one step ahead of us.

727
36:24.840 --> 36:27.450
Comrade Mao Zedong's working ability is beyond doubt.

728
36:27.450 --> 36:29.300
I've sent someone to deliver a letter

729
36:29.300 --> 36:30.680
asking him to prepare a detailed report

730
36:30.680 --> 36:32.510
on the situation in Yudu.

731
36:38.690 --> 36:44.450
[Yudu, Ganzhou, Jiangxi]

732
36:46.180 --> 36:47.110
Is anyone there?

733
36:47.970 --> 36:49.700
Give me something to eat.

734
36:56.050 --> 36:57.650
Is there any kind soul

735
36:58.450 --> 37:00.570
who can give me something to eat?

736
37:03.650 --> 37:04.740
Is anyone there?

737
37:30.170 --> 37:31.220
I'm exhausted.

738
37:33.390 --> 37:34.450
Give me some water.

739
37:41.240 --> 37:42.170
Where's the map?

740
37:42.540 --> 37:44.630
Hurry up and mark those two roads.

741
37:57.670 --> 38:00.340
This road is guarded by some troops.

742
38:00.440 --> 38:02.490
Did you get a clear look at how many men there were?

743
38:02.490 --> 38:04.660
They only have one company left.

744
38:04.780 --> 38:05.900
What about weapons?

745
38:05.900 --> 38:07.090
Only twenty or thirty rifles.

746
38:07.090 --> 38:09.780
The rest are spears and broadswords.

747
38:09.830 --> 38:10.890
This intelligence

748
38:11.020 --> 38:13.750
should earn us a hefty reward when we report back.

749
38:16.480 --> 38:19.210
From Guangdong-Jiangxi to southern Jiangxi,

750
38:19.820 --> 38:21.650
Chinese Soviet chairmen come and go,

751
38:21.650 --> 38:23.650
but the Soviet government remains.

752
38:23.700 --> 38:26.010
Comrade Zhong Shibin, how have you been?

753
38:26.220 --> 38:27.950
I'm doing very well, Chairman.

754
38:28.010 --> 38:30.420
The government of Jiangxi's southern province was only established a little over two months ago.

755
38:30.420 --> 38:32.010
There's so much to do,

756
38:32.170 --> 38:33.740
and we're certainly facing quite a few problems.

757
38:33.740 --> 38:35.470
It's perfect that you're here.

758
38:35.490 --> 38:36.570
I must seize the opportunity

759
38:36.570 --> 38:37.940
to ask for your advice.

760
38:38.650 --> 38:39.910
Rather than asking me,

761
38:40.560 --> 38:41.820
why not ask the people?

762
38:42.570 --> 38:45.650
How about this? Go and gather

763
38:46.050 --> 38:49.700
the cadres from the village, township, and district Chinese Soviets.

764
38:49.700 --> 38:52.360
Also invite some poor peasant representatives

765
38:52.380 --> 38:54.130
and handicraft workers.

766
38:54.700 --> 38:57.340
After I've gone out to investigate the situation,

767
38:57.340 --> 38:59.300
we'll set a time for a discussion.

768
38:59.700 --> 39:00.300
Okay.

769
39:00.450 --> 39:01.130
Report!

770
39:03.600 --> 39:04.400
Chairman Mao,

771
39:06.420 --> 39:09.080
here is a letter for you from Vice Chairman Zhou.

772
39:33.140 --> 39:34.870
Please tell Vice Chairman Zhou

773
39:35.490 --> 39:38.220
that I will complete the task as soon as possible.

774
39:38.220 --> 39:38.900
Yes.

775
39:41.370 --> 39:43.970
There's one more item to add to the discussion.

776
39:44.340 --> 39:45.670
Go ahead with your work.

777
39:47.860 --> 39:48.710
Chairman Mao.

778
39:48.930 --> 39:50.660
Chairman Mao, are you alright?

779
39:52.000 --> 39:52.850
I'm fine.

780
39:53.860 --> 39:54.860
I'm fine.

781
39:55.300 --> 39:56.430
You say you're fine,

782
39:56.660 --> 39:58.700
but looking at your physique.

783
39:58.720 --> 40:01.340
You look much thinner than you did back in Huichang.

784
40:01.340 --> 40:06.010
Losing a little weight will keep me more vigorous.

785
41:15.700 --> 41:16.300
Who is it?

786
41:16.320 --> 41:17.910
There's a spy!

787
41:17.940 --> 41:18.780
Catch him quickly!

788
41:18.780 --> 41:20.380
Someone come quickly!

789
41:20.820 --> 41:22.530
Someone come quickly! Is anyone there?

790
41:22.530 --> 41:23.300
Stop!

791
41:24.130 --> 41:26.380
There's a spy!

792
41:27.080 --> 41:28.260
Over there! Chase him!

793
41:28.260 --> 41:29.220
Hurry up and chase him!

794
41:29.220 --> 41:29.530
Quick!

795
41:29.530 --> 41:30.740
Someone come quickly!

796
41:30.740 --> 41:32.800
Someone come quickly! There's a spy!

797
41:34.030 --> 41:35.030
Chairman Mao,

798
41:35.700 --> 41:37.900
I escaped from my hometown in Xingguo.

799
41:38.090 --> 41:41.150
Our village was burned down by the Huanxiang Regiment,

800
41:41.450 --> 41:43.940
Many of my fellow villagers were killed.

801
41:44.540 --> 41:46.870
My father and my mother

802
41:47.650 --> 41:49.220
were tied to a tree

803
41:49.570 --> 41:51.300
and burned alive.

804
41:52.420 --> 41:53.570
They even said

805
41:53.970 --> 41:55.260
they'd burn the grass,

806
41:55.740 --> 41:56.900
cut the stones,

807
41:58.010 --> 41:59.490
and wipe out the people.

808
42:03.340 --> 42:07.050
Don't cry.

809
42:12.170 --> 42:12.940
Chairman Mao,

810
42:12.940 --> 42:15.130
we caught two spies from the Blue Shirts Society.

811
42:15.130 --> 42:16.190
Thanks to this kid.

812
42:16.340 --> 42:18.300
Here's the intelligence we seized.

813
42:18.300 --> 42:20.630
The spies have already infiltrated Yudu.

814
42:26.450 --> 42:29.340
Please take the boy

815
42:30.200 --> 42:32.390
to Comrade Zhong Shibin.

816
42:32.740 --> 42:33.650
Tell him

817
42:34.150 --> 42:37.680
the boy's parents were cadres of our Chinese Soviet government

818
42:38.080 --> 42:39.370
and died as martyrs.

819
42:39.930 --> 42:42.930
Ask them to settle the kid down well.

820
42:43.340 --> 42:45.740
Rest assured, Chairman Mao. Leave it to us.

821
42:47.820 --> 42:50.780
He will stay with me tonight.

822
42:51.190 --> 42:51.830
Yes.

823
43:00.060 --> 43:01.110
Sit here.
